course: dictionary
lesson: 9419
title: Informal words and their meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are informal. People use them in relaxed, everyday talk, not in formal writing such as a school report. Informal words can also have more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one. «The picture's a bit squiffy» means the picture is crooked, not straight on the wall.
explain: Ask yourself what the rest of the sentence tells you. A picture hangs on a wall, so squiffy must describe how it hangs. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The picture's a bit crooked» still makes sense, so you have found it.
explain: Squiffy has another meaning that is for grown-ups, about drinks, so leave that one alone. Use the clues in the sentence to choose the right meaning.
fact: Squiffy is an informal word, used in everyday British talk rather than in formal writing.
fact: «Squiffy» means crooked, not straight, as in «The picture's a bit squiffy».
fact: «Squiffy» can also mean slightly drunk, which is an adult word, so it is one for grown-ups.
fact: Squiffy is an adjective: squiffier and squiffiest compare how crooked something is.
fact: Informal words can have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
exercise: «The picture's a bit squiffy on the wall.» What does squiffy mean here? | Wet through | Shiny and brand new | *Crooked, not straight | Very loud
exercise: Mum says her handwriting is squiffy today. What does squiffy suggest? | Bright and colourful | Neat and tidy | *Wonky and uneven | Very fast
exercise: Squiffy is an informal word. What does informal mean? | *Used in relaxed, everyday talk, not in formal writing | Used only in official letters | Written in very old books | Used only by scientists
test: Ella says, «The tower is squiffy», meaning it leans. Which word fits best instead of squiffy? | Silent | *Leaning | Empty | Shiny
test: Which meaning of squiffy fits best in «The shelf is squiffy, so the books keep sliding off»? | Very heavy | *Crooked, not straight | Full of water | Clean and polished
exam: Which sentence uses squiffy to mean crooked? | *The clock on the wall is squiffy, so I will straighten it | We ate a squiffy lunch in the park | The puppy was squiffy and happy | The bus was squiffy after the bell rang
